      "requirement": "Inactive refused row still honors stop",
      "topology": "dependent",
      "fixture": "portable",
      "tests": [
        {
          "crate": "arroyo-controller",
          "name": "inactive_refused_row_honors_stop",
          "kind": "test",
          "path": "crates/arroyo-controller/src/states/mod.rs"
        }
      ],
      "distinct_path": "The fixture now gives the running job the state_context.leader a leader-mode row carries, so run_to_completion rebuilds a real LeaderManager against a real leader before the job's first state \u2014 the same reconnect production makes. The row then asserts the stop's last two status writes as one closed-form pair per topology: controller mode funnels every stop mode through Stopping before Stopped, because that is where this controller tears the workers down; worker-leader mode reaches Stopped straight from CheckpointStopping for a checkpoint stop, because the leader does the teardown and LeaderCheckpointStopping only waits for it to report JobStopped. The worker-leader cell therefore proves the job stopped through the leader, not merely that the row ran again."
    },
