        }
      ],
      "note": "Multi-test cell; it passes as a group. M11.T26m declared the controller control `a_busy_worker_phase_is_retried_under_the_same_start_admission` a PRE-ACTIVATION CONTROL ONLY, and M11.T26h's activation change removed it: it asserted that the fan-out retries the same identifier under the same admission after an `Aborted`, which is the reading M11.D39e(iii) replaces. `transport_settlement` no longer takes a mode and answers `Definitive` for `Aborted`, so the control could only have passed by keeping the mechanism it was a control for. Its half of the requirement \u2014 the controller's reading of a busy worker's answer \u2014 is carried by `busy_aborted_settles_no_apply_without_ambiguous_reconcile`, which asserts the stronger fact: exactly one START reaches the worker, the identifier is accounted for by an authoritative response, and the attempt ends as a retryable scheduling error so that only a LATER scheduling attempt may try again. The landed worker-side no-apply proof is unchanged."
    },
