      "note": "M11.T26m declared the control `a_permanently_unsettled_start_execution_ends_the_fan_out_and_releases_the_admission` a PRE-ACTIVATION CONTROL ONLY, and M11.T26h's activation change removed it. It asserted that budget exhaustion RELEASES the job's lifecycle authority \u2014 observed through `RefusalGate::admit_publication`, which the same change removed \u2014 and after activation budget exhaustion must enter durable `Fencing` instead, holding the authority until the obligation is discharged. The requirement 'a permanently unsettled start ends the fan-out safely' is carried whole by `permanently_unsettled_start_enters_durable_fencing`, which asserts the bounded terminal path AND the durable obligation the release used to skip; `budget_exhaustion_transfers_into_token_free_fencing_without_publishing_or_rescheduling` covers the same transfer at the phase seam."
